    "**Buffer Pathway:** When **%@** is present, **%@** tends to be suppressed. This suggests one acts as a protective buffer or compensation mechanism for the other." : {
      "comment" : "A description of a buffer pathway in a psychological network. The first argument is the name of the first node in the edge. The second argument is the name of the second node",
      "isCommentAutoGenerated" : true,
      "localizations" : {
        "en" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "new",
            "value" : "**Buffer Pathway:** When **%1$@** is present, **%2$@** tends to be suppressed. This suggests one acts as a protective buffer or compensation mechanism for the other."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "**Trigger Pathway:** When **%@** increases, **%@** tends to rise as well. This coupling suggests they reinforce each other directly in your coping patterns." : {
